# Worker judge

Import HostTools from "./host_tools.lg".
Import NodeRecord from "./node_record.lg".
Import WorkRecord from "./work_record.lg".
Import VerdictRecord from "./verdict_record.lg".
Import TrailMemory from "./trail_memory.lg".
Import Extraction from "./extraction.lg".
Import VernacularCommand from "./vernacular_command.lg".
Import SubmissionPolicy from "./submission_policy.lg".
Import ProofDocument from "./proof_document.lg".
Import PromptRoles from "./prompt_roles.lg".
Import Verifier from "./verifier.lg".
Import ArtifactRules from "./artifact_rules.lg".
Import CoordinatorWire from "./coordinator_wire.lg".

A worker judges its own answer with the kernel before it claims anything, as the
trusted verifier will again: a proof (`prove`, `repair`, `decompose`) is
assembled onto the statement and checked under the acceptance policy; a
`formalize` answer is checked as a statement and, when it checks, proposed as a
draft for review; a `review` answer is read for its verdict, which only
`faithful` makes an agreement. The approach is fingerprinted from the kind, the
statement, the strategy and the proof's tactic skeleton.

## A WorkJudged has:
    a verdict, which is Verdict.
    a fingerprint, which is Text.
    an extraction, which is Extraction.
    a document, which is Text.
    a draft, which is Option of StatementDraft.

## Note
A review: its verdict line read, its issues kept as the detail. Its approach is
the reviewer's own (`reviewer` names the contributor and model), so a second
independent rejection is never mistaken for a repeat of the first.

## To judgeReview (st: Statement, strategyId: Text, content: Text, reviewer: Text) -> WorkJudged:
    Let x be extractBlock(content, "review").
    Let word be lower(fieldLine(x's block, "verdict")).
    Let mutable detail be "the reviewer says " + word + "; issues: " + fieldLine(x's block, "issues").
    If x's problem is not equal to "":
        Set detail to x's problem.
    Let v be newVerdict(reviewVerdictKind(word), 0, "", [], detail).
    Let fp be approachFingerprint("review", st's sha256, strategyId, "review " + word + " by " + reviewer).
    Return a new WorkJudged with verdict v and fingerprint fp and extraction x and document "" and draft none.

## Note
The answer to a unit of `kind` on `st`, judged.

## To judgeWork (kind: Text, st: Statement, strategyId: Text, content: Text, reviewer: Text) -> WorkJudged:
    If kind is equal to "review":
        Return judgeReview(st, strategyId, content, reviewer).
    Let x be extractSubmission(content).
    Let mutable subject be st's sha256.
    If kind is equal to "formalize":
        Set subject to st's problemId.
    Let mutable j be a new WorkJudged with verdict refusedSubmissionVerdict([x's problem]) and extraction x and document "" and draft none.
    Set j's fingerprint to approachFingerprint(kind, subject, strategyId, "no-submission").
    If x's problem is not equal to "":
        Return j.
    Set j's fingerprint to approachFingerprint(kind, subject, strategyId, submissionSkeleton(x's block)).
    If kind is equal to "formalize":
        Set j's document to x's block.
        Set j's verdict to judgeStatement(defaultToolchain(), x's block, st's goalName).
        If j's verdict's kind is equal to "verified":
            Set j's draft to some (a new StatementDraft with document x's block and goalName st's goalName and route "C").
        Return j.
    Set j's document to assembleProofDocument(st's document, x's block, proofNameFor(st's goalName)).
    Set j's verdict to judgeSubmission(defaultToolchain(), st's document, st's goalName, x's block).
    Return j.

## Note
An artifact under the hash of its text.

## To artifactOfText (name: Text, text: Text) -> ArtifactUpload:
    Return a new ArtifactUpload with sha256 contentSha(text) and name name and text text.

## Note
The files an attempt hands over, in the order its trail entry lists them: the
request, the answer, then — when the answer held a block — the submission and
the document the kernel checked, then the verdict.

## To workArtifacts (requestJson: Text, answer: Text, j: WorkJudged) -> Seq of ArtifactUpload:
    Let mutable out be [artifactOfText("prompt.json", requestJson), artifactOfText("answer.txt", answer)].
    If j's extraction's problem is equal to "" and j's document is not equal to "":
        Push artifactOfText("submission.lg", j's extraction's block) to out.
        Push artifactOfText("document.lg", j's document) to out.
    Push artifactOfText("verdict.json", toJson_Verdict(j's verdict)) to out.
    Return out.

## Note
The hashes of a list of artifacts, in order.

## To artifactShasOf (xs: Seq of ArtifactUpload) -> Seq of Text:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for a in xs:
        Push a's sha256 to out.
    Return out.

## Note
The judgement of a call never made because the budget could not hold it.

## To budgetJudged (u: WorkUnit, strategyId: Text, stop: Text) -> WorkJudged:
    Let x be a new Extraction with block "" and summary "the budget stopped the call before it was made" and suggestions [] and problem "no answer was bought".
    Let v be newVerdict("budget_exhausted", 0, stop, [], "the contributor's budget could not hold the call's worst case").
    Let fp be approachFingerprint(u's kind, u's problemId, strategyId, "budget stop").
    Return a new WorkJudged with verdict v and fingerprint fp and extraction x and document "" and draft none.
